{"id": "travel-gifts-missing-from-form-700", "title": "Trips filed as gifts of travel, missing from the officials’ Form 700s", "seconds": 149.1, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "ccf70d78372ae235", "words": 399, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "When someone else pays for an elected officer’s trip, San Francisco keeps two records:", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.43, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "A trip paid by someone else", "sub": "two records of one gift"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.5, 0.77, 1.16, 1.28, 1.37, 1.71, 2.11, 2.89, 3.14, 3.71, 4.01, 4.29]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "a gift-of-travel form before the trip, and the yearly statement called Form 700.", "t0": 5.43, "t1": 10.42, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["before the trip", "gift-of-travel form"], "b": ["once a year", "Form 700 statement"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.17, 0.81, 1.09, 1.38, 1.47, 2.08, 2.24, 2.33, 2.63, 3.01, 3.6, 4.27, 4.63]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "established[0]"], "text": "Of 124 trips that can be checked, how many are missing from the Form 700?", "t0": 10.54, "t1": 16.66, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "124 trips that can be checked", "sub": "filed 2015 to 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.35, 0.67, 1.22, 1.65, 1.8, 1.94, 2.05, 3.01, 3.22, 3.46, 3.57, 3.93, 4.09, 4.2, 4.66, 4.95]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[0]"], "text": "8 trips, worth 15,718.38 dollars.", "t0": 16.66, "t1": 22.42, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$15,718.38", "label": "8 trips, 7 elected officers", "sub": "not on the statement on file"}, "emph": ["8 trips"], "wt": [0.04, 0.29, 1.21, 1.52, 2.08, 2.6, 2.86, 3.26, 3.78, 4.64, 4.86, 5.34]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 22.94, "t1": 24.61, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.33, 0.4, 0.99, 1.17, 1.24]}, {"scene": "match", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[0]", "story[1]"], "text": "Most do match: 116 of 124, or 93.5 percent.", "t0": 24.83, "t1": 31.76, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "116", "label": "of 124 trips also on the officer’s Form 700", "sub": "93.5%"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.64, 0.85, 1.83, 2.05, 2.33, 3.02, 3.21, 3.39, 3.71, 4.97, 5.17, 5.84, 6.12, 6.46]}, {"scene": "match", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[4]", "links[3]"], "text": "The gaps are few and mostly small. What they show is that nobody compares the two filings.", "t0": 31.88, "t1": 37.12, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "nobody compares the two filings"}, "emph": ["nobody compares"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.45, 0.64, 0.99, 1.15, 1.55, 2.61, 2.77, 2.93, 3.24, 3.35, 3.52, 3.87, 4.4, 4.5, 4.69]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "story[2]"], "text": "The clearest pair is from March 2023: two trips filed by Supervisor Matthew Dorsey.", "t0": 37.34, "t1": 42.62, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Supervisor Matthew Dorsey", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "two trips, March 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.52, 0.86, 0.98, 1.15, 1.46, 1.74, 2.89, 3.12, 3.47, 3.84, 4.01, 4.55, 4.85]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "One paid by the Chamber of Commerce Foundation, 4,000 dollars.", "t0": 42.74, "t1": 46.78, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Chamber of Commerce Foundation", "$4,000.00"], "b": ["CARECEN", "$1,572.02"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.56, 0.68, 0.77, 1.06, 1.17, 1.51, 2.43, 2.67, 3.03]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "One by CARECEN, 1,572.02.", "t0": 46.78, "t1": 51.3, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Chamber of Commerce Foundation", "$4,000.00"], "b": ["CARECEN", "$1,572.02"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.26, 0.43, 1.39, 1.63, 2.03, 2.28, 2.82, 3.53, 3.8, 4.13]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]", "timeline[3]", "timeline[4]"], "text": "Supervisors Joel Engardio and Hillary Ronen were on those trips, and listed them on their statements.", "t0": 51.42, "t1": 56.7, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Joel Engardio", "sub": "listed the Chamber trip"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Hillary Ronen", "sub": "listed the CARECEN trip"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Matthew Dorsey", "sub": "filed both trips"}], "kicker": "Same trips"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.76, 1.09, 1.7, 1.86, 2.23, 2.55, 2.74, 2.85, 3.07, 3.78, 3.98, 4.3, 4.47, 4.56, 4.7]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[1]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Dorsey’s own statement for 2023 lists gifts. And travel payments?", "t0": 56.82, "t1": 61.75, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Dorsey’s statement for 2023, filing 211551891", "text": "3 gifts (each printed twice in the open data) and 0 travel entries", "mark": "0 travel entries"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.42, 0.62, 1.1, 1.25, 1.52, 2.03, 2.3, 3.32, 3.51, 3.81]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "Not one.", "t0": 61.75, "t1": 62.43, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "0", "label": "travel payments on Dorsey’s 2023 statement", "sub": "3 gifts, each printed twice"}, "emph": ["Not one"], "wt": [0.04, 0.33]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[3]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "The largest single gap is older.", "t0": 63.05, "t1": 65.51, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Supervisor Malia Cohen", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "Dublin, London and Oslo, from May 23, 2015", "chip": "$3,820.00"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.53, 0.85, 1.29, 1.5]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[3]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "In May 2015, Supervisor Malia Cohen filed a trip abroad.", "t0": 65.51, "t1": 69.34, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Supervisor Malia Cohen", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "Dublin, London and Oslo, from May 23, 2015", "chip": "$3,820.00"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.47, 0.71, 1.56, 2.08, 2.43, 2.83, 3.12, 3.18, 3.38]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "story[3]"], "text": "Dublin, London and Oslo, worth 3,820 dollars,", "t0": 69.46, "t1": 73.91, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The biosolids digester project", "sub": "sewer technology, in her district"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.47, 0.83, 0.95, 1.68, 1.97, 2.35, 2.85, 3.06, 3.34, 3.66]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "story[3]"], "text": "to see technology for a sewer project in her district.", "t0": 73.91, "t1": 76.76, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The biosolids digester project", "sub": "sewer technology, in her district"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.19, 0.44, 1.05, 1.22, 1.32, 1.67, 2.1, 2.22, 2.37]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "Her 2015 statement doesn’t list it. And who paid? The open data doesn’t say.", "t0": 76.88, "t1": 82.38, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Cohen’s statement for 2015", "text": "One travel payment listed: a different trip. Who paid for this one is not in the open data.", "mark": "a different trip"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.52, 0.97, 1.42, 1.78, 2.06, 2.72, 2.88, 3.08, 4.02, 4.21, 4.46, 4.74, 5.07]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[2]", "timeline[2]"], "text": "In 2017 and 2018, she voted for two of that project’s contracts.", "t0": 82.5, "t1": 86.49, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Biosolids contracts Cohen voted for", "rows": [["Brown and Caldwell, 2017", "$153,500,000 ceiling"], ["Arcadis U.S., Inc., 2018", "$42,000,000 ceiling"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.41, 0.98, 1.1, 1.4, 1.9, 2.1, 2.37, 2.51, 2.77, 2.85, 3.01, 3.42]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Why does it matter who paid?", "t0": 86.61, "t1": 88.66, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a later vote on the project’s contracts would be a vote on a giver’s matter"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.44, 0.55, 0.83, 1.01]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "If a firm with a stake paid, those votes would be on a giver’s matter.", "t0": 88.66, "t1": 92.55, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a later vote on the project’s contracts would be a vote on a giver’s matter"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.32, 0.65, 0.8, 0.87, 1.18, 2.03, 2.42, 2.74, 2.9, 3.04, 3.16, 3.21, 3.56]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "timeline[5]"], "text": "City Attorney David Chiu filed three trips from the Rodel Institute in 2024.", "t0": 92.77, "t1": 97.35, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "City Attorney David Chiu", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "three Rodel Institute trips, 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.68, 1.02, 1.44, 1.79, 2.1, 2.43, 2.56, 2.65, 2.99, 3.51, 3.66, 3.98]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "His statement lists the January and December trips. Which one is missing?", "t0": 97.47, "t1": 102.04, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Chiu’s statement for 2024, filing 213951314", "text": "12 gift and 3 travel entries: the January and December trips", "mark": "January and December"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.61, 0.86, 0.97, 1.49, 1.58, 1.95, 3.0, 3.23, 3.34, 3.44]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "August, worth 3,143.82 dollars.", "t0": 102.04, "t1": 107.69, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$3,143.82", "label": "the trip from August 14, 2024", "sub": "not on his 2024 statement"}, "emph": ["August"], "wt": [0.04, 0.94, 1.26, 1.64, 2.17, 2.45, 2.82, 3.3, 4.08, 4.45, 5.09]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "Four more are from 2016 and 2017: David Campos,", "t0": 108.21, "t1": 112.71, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Trips of 2016 and 2017 with no matching entry", "rows": [["David Campos, Vancouver", "$300.00"], ["Jeff Sheehy, Washington, D.C.", "$841.08"], ["London Breed, New York", "$1,094.00"], ["Hillary Ronen, Austin", "$947.46"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.68, 0.86, 1.03, 1.31, 1.89, 2.06, 2.32, 3.42, 3.77]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "Jeff Sheehy, London Breed and Hillary Ronen.", "t0": 112.71, "t1": 115.64, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Trips of 2016 and 2017 with no matching entry", "rows": [["David Campos, Vancouver", "$300.00"], ["Jeff Sheehy, Washington, D.C.", "$841.08"], ["London Breed, New York", "$1,094.00"], ["Hillary Ronen, Austin", "$947.46"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.34, 1.21, 1.6, 1.99, 2.2, 2.56]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "timeline[1]"], "text": "Then Mayor Edwin Lee. His 10 trips of 2017 are on no statement at all.", "t0": 115.86, "t1": 121.1, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "10", "label": "trips filed by Mayor Edwin Lee in 2017", "sub": "$59,340.49, no Form 700 covering the year"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.67, 0.92, 1.2, 2.26, 2.49, 2.75, 3.09, 3.19, 3.43, 3.94, 4.1, 4.26, 4.5, 4.87, 4.97]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "Together, they were worth 59,340.49 dollars.", "t0": 121.22, "t1": 126.68, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "10", "label": "trips filed by Mayor Edwin Lee in 2017", "sub": "$59,340.49, no Form 700 covering the year"}, "emph": ["59,340.49"], "wt": [0.0, 0.75, 0.89, 1.02, 1.29, 1.92, 2.34, 2.67, 3.01, 3.34, 4.25, 4.45, 5.01]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why", "innocent[0]"], "text": "Why no statement? In December 2017, the Board recorded condolences on his passing.", "t0": 126.8, "t1": 133.57, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "December 2017", "sub": "the Board records condolences on the passing of Mayor Lee"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.66, 1.16, 2.69, 2.86, 3.26, 3.54, 4.52, 4.66, 5.01, 5.42, 6.07, 6.17, 6.31]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]", "innocent[0]"], "text": "The records don’t show whether a trip was repaid, or listed on an amended statement.", "t0": 133.79, "t1": 137.71, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Whether any officer repaid a trip", "Whether an amended statement exists", "That any vote was influenced by a trip"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.5, 0.69, 0.95, 1.2, 1.26, 1.48, 1.63, 2.49, 2.62, 2.93, 3.03, 3.11, 3.49]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? Each statement, any amendment, and the travel filings that name the payer.", "t0": 137.83, "t1": 143.07, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Each officer’s statement and any amendment, for each trip"}, {"who": "", "what": "The gift-of-travel filings themselves: payer, repayment"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.33, 0.57, 1.45, 1.81, 2.35, 2.62, 3.42, 3.57, 3.66, 3.95, 4.32, 4.49, 4.77, 4.88]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[0]"], "text": "No authority has made a finding about any of these filings.", "t0": 143.19, "t1": 146.01, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.72, 0.85, 1.01, 1.09, 1.48, 1.75, 1.97, 2.04, 2.24]}, {"scene": "close", 